<title>USA: Roth says US tax talks progress, still a way to go.</title>
<headline>Roth says US tax talks progress, still a way to go.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senate Finance Committee Chairman William Roth said Tuesday discussions between House and Senate Republicans on trying to craft a compromise tax cut bill were progressing, but still had a way to go.</p>
<p>&quot;We've had very positive discussions; we've made some real progress, and we still have a ways to go,&quot; Roth said.</p>
<p>The Delaware Republican said it was &quot;entirely possible&quot; there could be a unified Republican position on the tax bill by the end of the day.</p>
</text>
